  "experiments": {
    "setup": "Excerpts of the test scene (1344x768 -> 2016x1152, 24 fps): 2 s = 48 frames (sweep_2s) and 33 frames = one context window (sweep_33). WAN 2.2 T2V A14B low-noise fp8 + lightx2v 4-step LoRA v1.1 (low noise), shift 5, euler/simple, CFG 1, R9700, VRAM guard. PSNR after Lanczos downscale to 1344x768; sharpness = median Laplacian variance (Lanczos upscale of the source = 38).",
    "runs": [
      {
        "id": "A",
        "config": "whole frame, denoise 0.30, 4 steps, windows 33/8 standard_uniform, 48 frames",
        "s_per_step": 280.6,
        "psnr_db": 16.4,
        "sharpness": 66,
        "result": "re-draws the scene: face identity, sign lettering and the pink bear change (start sigma 0.69)"
      },
      {
        "id": "W1_d0.15",
        "config": "whole frame, denoise 0.15, 4 steps, 33 frames",
        "s_per_step": 95.4,
        "psnr_db": 20.3,
        "sharpness": 58
      },
      {
        "id": "W1_d0.20",
        "config": "whole frame, denoise 0.20, 4 steps, 33 frames",
        "s_per_step": 95.8,
        "psnr_db": 18.7,
        "sharpness": 62
      },
      {
        "id": "T1",
        "config": "832x480 tiles, denoise 0.20, 4 steps",
        "s_per_step": 43.0,
        "psnr_db": 19.9,
        "sharpness": 66,
        "result": "no visible tile seams; finer facade detail than the whole frame; 2.2x faster"
      },
      {
        "id": "T2",
        "config": "1280x720 tiles, denoise 0.20, 4 steps",
        "s_per_step": 73.1,
        "psnr_db": 19.8,
        "sharpness": 63
      },
      {
        "id": "T3",
        "config": "832x480 tiles, denoise 0.15, 4 steps",
        "s_per_step": 43.0,
        "psnr_db": 21.4,
        "sharpness": 61,
        "median_abs_error": 14.1
      },
      {
        "id": "T4 (shipped sampling)",
        "config": "832x480 tiles, denoise 0.15, 2 steps",
        "s_per_step": 43.1,
        "psnr_db": 21.5,
        "sharpness": 63,
        "median_abs_error": 14.0,
        "result": "visually equal to 4 steps at half the time"
      },
      {
        "id": "T6",
        "config": "832x480 tiles, denoise 0.10, 2 steps",
        "s_per_step": 43.1,
        "psnr_db": 23.9,
        "sharpness": 55,
        "median_abs_error": 10.6,
        "result": "most faithful (sign lettering kept), less new detail"
      },
      {
        "id": "T7",
        "config": "as T4 with a descriptive prompt (eye colour, make-up, clothing)",
        "psnr_db": 21.5,
        "sharpness": 63,
        "result": "no visible difference to the generic prompt at this denoise"
      },
      {
        "id": "V21",
        "config": "as T4 with WAN 2.1 T2V 14B fp8 + lightx2v T2V 14B cfg/step-distill v2 LoRA",
        "s_per_step": 51.3,
        "psnr_db": 27.4,
        "sharpness": 49,
        "result": "same graph works; 2.1 changes much less (keeps the blue eyes and sign text) and adds less detail than the 2.2 low-noise expert"
      }
    ],
    "first_frame": {
      "finding": "WAN re-draws the start of every clip more strongly: abs. error to the source 24.9 at frame 0 falling to ~17 by frame 8 (T1); the plain VAE round trip (denoise 0.01) is flat at 3.4 - the sampler, not the VAE, causes it (the first latent stands for a single frame).",
      "fix": "5 lead-in frames rendered along and dropped (DaWVULoadBlock lead_frames): frame 0 error 24.9 -> 15.4, jump into frame 1 +3.8 -> +1.0, clip median 17.0 -> 14.4 (T5 vs T1, same settings)."
    },
    "memory": {
      "core_loaders": "UNETLoader/CLIPLoader: main run 39.9 -> 90.7 GB commit (UMT5 +12, model file mapping + frames +25, model to GPU +10, decode +5); 2496x1408 run already 93.5 GB before the decode (run stopped, ~109 GB expected)",
      "read_only_loaders": "DaWVUReadOnlyUNETLoader/DaWVUReadOnlyCLIPLoader (h3_highres read-only mapping): bit-identical film; commit peak main 77.5 GB, two blocks 80.9 GB, 2496x1408 / 209 frames 97.2 GB (baseline 34.9 GB)",
      "second_model": "101.2 of 105.4 GB while a second 14B model (the I2V speed probe) stayed cached in RAM next to the T2V model",
      "tiles_vram": "whole-frame windows loaded the model partially (845 MB lowvram); with 832x480 tiles the VRAM budget is per tile and the model loads completely"
    },
    "speed_probe_i2v": "WAN 2.2 I2V low-noise used only as a speed proxy before the T2V download finished: 232-242 s per step for 2 whole-frame windows; interrupted",
    "block_border": "two blocks inside one shot (3/2/4 s): face consistent, blurry neon lettering changes letters (seam excess +0.57); existing music-video scenes: mean 7.0 s, 70 of 126 > 7 s, none > 10 s -> shipped blocks 7/2/10 s",
    "mouth": "2496x1408 run: mouth opening/closing in sync with the source, a lopsided talking mouth becomes a symmetric smile (frames 96-102)"
  },
  "visual_review": "1:1 crops (frames 38/76/114 of the main run; 51/102/153 of the memory run): clearly more detail than Lanczos - balcony railings, window frames, ivy, bricks, skin texture, single hair strands; the motion-blurred face of the source (frame 76) becomes sharp. Sign lettering is kept (INAAG); lips and irises become more saturated/darker. Mouth opening and closing stays in sync with the source, but a lopsided talking mouth becomes a symmetric smile (memory run, frames 96-102). Two-block run: the face stays consistent across the block border, blurry neon lettering changes letters (seam excess +0.57, inside a block ~0).",
